This optional Python plugin uses BabelDOC and PyMuPDF and communicates with
the main application through the documented stdio protocol. It is packaged
separately from the main application. Its distribution includes server.py and
requirements.lock; these files alone are not all corresponding source for a
bundled Python runtime and its dependencies.

Third-party files, including asset-licenses/, retain their original notices
and licenses. Built components include THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt and
PYTHON-LICENSE.txt; asset archives include their own license directory.
Upstream references: https://pypi.org/project/BabelDOC/0.6.4/ and
https://pymupdf.io/licensing .
